WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.530
What would happen if humankind became extinct
at any moment?

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:09.820
I bet that, among you, lovers of the post-apocalyptic
genre will have already foretasted this scenario,

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:14.750
whether it be by a nuclear winter, a giant
tidal wave as in Roland Emmerich's 2012 or

00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:17.650
an unstoppable pandemic as in The Last of
Us.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:22.990
The result, however, would be similar: ruined
buildings devoured by climbing plants, streets

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:26.119
occupied by car wrecks, animals and stores
pillaged.

00:00:26.119 --> 00:00:31.720
A Fallout-like atmosphere, which writer Alan
Weisman describes in his essay The World Without

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:32.720
Us.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.840
After all, it’s easy to imagine a completely
abandoned urban setting.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.810
That’s what we are talking about today:
ghost towns.

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:43.750
They can be found everywhere, there are intact
ones and crumbling ones, and as we’ll see

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:46.050
shortly, their origins are indeed varied.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:51.050
For American writer Lambert Florin, a ghost
town is "a ghostly semblance of what it itself

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.050
used to be."

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:56.969
That is why my first thought goes to Pryp"jat,
in the Ukrainian oblast of Kiev, evacuated

00:00:56.969 --> 00:01:02.870
on April 28, 1986, the day after the well-known
Chernobyl nuclear disaster.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:07.000
To date, radiation levels have stabilized
thanks in part to the new protective arch

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.450
surrounding the reactor.

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:13.180
To the point that the site attracts tourists
from all over the world thanks to the famous

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:17.700
ferris wheel and structures that have remained
literally forty years old.

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:22.259
Well, Pryp"jat leads the way for us to talk
about the first reason why a city should be

00:01:22.259 --> 00:01:23.520
abandoned: a disaster.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:29.909
This expanse of ash, sand and gutted dwellings
surrounded by tropical nature is-or rather,

00:01:29.909 --> 00:01:34.640
was-Plymouth, the capital and main port of
entry to the island of Montserrat, a British

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.450
overseas possession located in the Lesser
Antilles archipelago.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:43.890
To the south rises the Soufrière Hills, a
volcano just over 1,000 meters high that had

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:50.250
been dormant for centuries until it erupted
on several occasions beginning in July 1995,

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:55.270
flooding a large area of the island, including
the capital, with debris and pyroclastic flows.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:02:02.189
Two years later, on June 25, 1997, a new devastating
eruption destroyed 80 percent of Plymouth,

00:02:02.189 --> 00:02:03.189
burying it under ash.

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:08.650
The volcanic material consolidated to the
point that it became unremovable except with

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:13.580
the help of explosives or bulldozers, which
was impractical given the cost.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:18.680
Therefore, after the British Navy ship, HMS
Liverpool, had evacuated the inhabitants to

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:24.190
other islands including Antigua and Guadeloupe,
most of them, chose to emigrate to the UK

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:29.129
or to Brades, the new de facto capital, now
the seat of administrative offices.

00:02:29.129 --> 00:02:33.910
Officially, the capital still remains Plymouth,
awaiting the completion of the Little Bay

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:35.740
port in the northwest.

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:38.319
And what to do with a wasteland in the meantime?

00:02:38.319 --> 00:02:40.670
Montserrat's government has clear ideas.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:46.060
In 2016, then-Premier Donaldson Romeo declared,
"we have learned to live with the volcano

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.800
[...], it’s time to convert ash into money."

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:49.800
A metaphor?

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:50.800
Well, not so much.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:56.470
As early as 2010, trucks and bulldozers had
begun removing sand from the so-called exclusion

00:02:56.470 --> 00:03:01.670
zone, that is the inaccessible area-in Plymouth,
to sell it on the international market as

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:03.100
construction material.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:09.500
The volcano itself has also come in handy,
so much so that between 2012 and 2017 the

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:14.230
island's government drilled three wells for
geothermal energy extraction with financial

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:20.700
help from the British Crown and wants to build
a fourth facility by 2024 right in the exclusion

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.700
zone.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:26.360
This has coincided with the advent of tourists
and lovers of apocalyptic scenarios, who are

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:30.030
interested in what is now called "the Pompeii
of the Caribbean."

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:34.879
And from the combo of vacations and natural
disasters...here comes a ghost resort.

00:03:34.879 --> 00:03:40.250
It’s Villa Epecuén, a land of architectural
skeletons, rotten trees, abandoned luggage

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:45.730
and wreckage of all kinds, which remained
submerged for a quarter of a century and resurfaced

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:50.180
only when the waters began to recede in the
summer of 2009.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:57.480
Beginning in 1921, the area, some 600km from
Buenos Aires, began to be occupied by vacation

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:04.640
homes, stores, clubs, and luxury hotels, and
by the 1970s, the huge flow of tourists, attracted

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:09.710
by the healing properties of Lake Epecuen's
waters, brought the picturesque spa town to

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:13.340
accommodate a population of more than 5,000.

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:18.670
Everything seemed to be going well, until
in November 1985, a sudden drop in atmospheric

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:24.370
pressure generated a so-called sessa phenomenon,
that is, a periodic wave motion, in the lake.

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:30.310
The latter broke the embankment built in 1978
to protect the village, and before long the

00:04:30.310 --> 00:04:36.190
area disappeared under 3 meters of water,
which then rose to 10 in 1993.

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:41.590
The drought of 2009 uncovered some of the
salt-bleached trees and structures, and among

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:48.060
the few still intact, a magnificent slaughterhouse
built by Argentine architect Francisco Salamone

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:49.110
stands out.

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:54.330
But there is a second reason that can lead
a city to mutate into a ghost town: the anticipation

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.710
of some disastrous event.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.360
Do you know Mel Gibson's The Passion of the
Christ?

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:04.310
The movie was shot in Craco, an ancient, now
uninhabited medieval village in southern Italy,

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:05.510
Matera province.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:10.950
First a huge landslide in 1963 that forced
the inhabitants to move downstream to Craco

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:17.290
Peschiera, then a flood in 1972 that prevented
the repopulation of the old town, and finally

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:22.840
the Irpinia earthquake in 1980 transformed
the village into a tourist attraction and

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:24.389
valuable movie set.

00:05:24.389 --> 00:05:29.729
The same happened to the Irish island settlement
of Great Blasket, inhabited for centuries

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:35.870
by a small community that reached 200 people
in the early 20th century but was evacuated

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:41.590
permanently by the government in November
1953 because of increasingly extreme weather

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:42.590
conditions.

00:05:42.590 --> 00:05:46.130
Fear of some unpleasant event has also reached
the Indonesian authorities.

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:52.319
The capital Jakarta is set to sink under water
by 2050, and this is due to the fact that

00:05:52.319 --> 00:05:58.580
the megacity, already washed by the Java Sea,
rests on swampy ground traversed by as many

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:00.319
as 13 rivers.

00:06:00.319 --> 00:06:05.720
It should come as no surprise that, due to
frequent flooding, in 2019 the local government

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:11.660
announced the construction of a new administrative
and political center, Nusantara, to be built

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:15.590
1,300 kilometers away on the island of Borneo.

00:06:15.590 --> 00:06:22.130
Of course, this move, with an estimated cost
of $32.4 billion, brings with it objections

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:27.419
of various kinds, from the choice of name
for the new capital to the environmental issue

00:06:27.419 --> 00:06:31.960
related to the deforestation of an area rich
in wildlife and rainforests.

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:37.150
But, for our purposes, it will be interesting
to observe the process of Jakarta's transition

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:41.569
from an overcrowded city housing 10 million
people into a ghost town.

00:06:41.569 --> 00:06:46.050
On closer inspection then, what defines an
abandoned town is also a sudden change in

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:48.310
pre-existing economic conditions.

00:06:48.310 --> 00:06:53.419
Those human settlements that arise as a result
of the industrial and demographic development

00:06:53.419 --> 00:06:59.210
of a given area, such as around a factory
system or a mine, take the name “boomtown”.

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:04.690
Think of urban centers such as Manchester
and Liverpool, which arose during the Industrial

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:10.639
Revolution, or Kiruna, in Lapland, created
in 1900 by the Swedish kingdom to exploit

00:07:10.639 --> 00:07:16.060
the nearby mine, which today supplies 80 percent
of the iron mined in Europe.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:21.730
In the 1970s, as the mine expanded both above
and below ground, several neighborhoods in

00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:26.090
the town were cleared and incorporated into
the expanding site.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:31.009
After all, this is also the inevitable fate
of any village in the proximity of any deposit.

00:07:31.009 --> 00:07:36.289
At the moment, the swedish government, in
order to prevent the prosecution of excavation,

00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:41.919
which is already responsible for several landslides
in the ground and collapse of structures,

00:07:41.919 --> 00:07:47.249
from endangering the safety of the inhabitants,
is implementing an ambitious - and expensive

00:07:47.249 --> 00:07:55.009
- plan to physically move and reassemble elsewhere
some 3,000 structures, 65 percent of the buildings

00:07:55.009 --> 00:07:56.340
in the entire town.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:08:01.330
And what happens if the activity around which
a boomtown revolves suddenly ceases?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:04.690
The example of the California town of Bodie
is illuminating.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:09.759
We are in the areas bordering the Sierra Nevada
mountain range, where huge amounts of gold

00:08:09.759 --> 00:08:14.180
were discovered beginning in the second half
of the 1800s (eighteen hundreds).

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:20.229
In 1859, a man named William or Wakeman S.
Bodey discovered a rich gold deposit about

00:08:20.229 --> 00:08:26.650
16 kilometers from Monoville and there founded
Bodie, a modest town of just a few houses,

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:30.600
about 20 miners and almost irrelevant mining
activity.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:35.430
This was because news of the discovery didn’t
spread far and took a back seat to the rapid

00:08:35.430 --> 00:08:39.640
development of the huge Comstock Lode mines
in Virginia City and Aurora.

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:44.830
When these deposits were later exhausted,
Bodie experienced its moment of glory, coming

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:52.100
to be home to some 10,000 inhabitants between
1879 and 1880, dozens of saloons, brothels,

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:58.160
opium dens, and a small Chinatown, eventually
earning its reputation as "shooters town",

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:00.980
because of the frequent gunfights on the city
streets.

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:07.010
In the early 1900s mining began to decline,
and the mine closed its doors for good in

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:12.560
1913, leading to a rapid decline in profits,
until even the Bodie and Benton Railroad slowly

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:13.850
became unused.

00:09:13.850 --> 00:09:19.530
The 50-kilometer rail line that, linking Bodie
to Mono Mills, ensured the mining town a steady

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:20.630
supply of lumber.

00:09:20.630 --> 00:09:26.940
A series of adverse circumstances then led
residents to abandon the area in 1942, and

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:33.420
since 1962 Bodie has been a tourist attraction
in a state of "arrested decay," consisting

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:38.320
of dusty wooden buildings, wrecked Chevrolets
and rusting electric generators.

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:43.500
The same fate happened to many other outposts
that sprang up during the gold rush period.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:47.500
But don't think that places devoted to various
mining activities escaped it.

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:52.350
The most problematic case is surely that of
Wittenoom, a former mining town in Western

00:09:52.350 --> 00:09:57.570
Australia that has earned the unpleasant nickname
of "the most contaminated site in the southern

00:09:57.570 --> 00:09:58.570
hemisphere."

00:09:58.570 --> 00:10:04.860
In fact, the 20,000 people who lived there
were evacuated in 1978 because the mining

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:12.541
of crocidolite, the deadliest type of asbestos,
from 1943 to 1966 contaminated the soil, led

00:10:12.541 --> 00:10:17.950
to the deaths of hundreds of people and increased
the risk of developing respiratory diseases

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:19.160
and cancers.

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:24.440
And over time, efforts to clean up and remove
3 million tons of toxic waste haven’t produced

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:26.120
the desired results.

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:30.490
An exclusion zone of 50 thousand hectares
of land is mentioned, but according to the

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:33.840
Australian government, the estimate could
be even worse.

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:39.870
Another deserted place is Kolmanskop, in southern
Namibia, a German architectural-style settlement

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:45.750
located on that portion of the Namib desert
that the German government in the early 1900s

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:50.910
classified as a "Sperrgebiet"- reserved area
- dedicated to diamond exploration.

00:10:50.910 --> 00:10:55.580
In 1954 the diamonds ended and with them,
so did the mining.

00:10:55.580 --> 00:11:01.350
Today, the desert has reclaimed its dominance
over houses, dance halls, casinos and even

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:03.370
Africa's first tramway.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:08.160
Then taking a huge leap northward in latitude,
we find a very unique boomtown: we are talking

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:13.700
about Pyramiden, an old Swedish outpost dating
back to 1910 located in the Norwegian archipelago

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:16.420
of Svalbard and intended for coal production.

00:11:16.420 --> 00:11:21.880
It was donated to the Soviet Union in 1927,
becoming the second Russian outpost on the

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:25.790
larger island of Spitsbergen, along with the
Barentsburg outpost.

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:31.370
This small 2-square-kilometer urban center,
operating under the control of Soviet mining

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:37.490
giant Arktikugol, was home to a community
of Russian miners for decades, and its 60

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:42.480
km of mine shafts continued to operate until
the early 1990s.

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:47.140
But reduced production combined with the costs
and logistics required to maintain such a

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:52.350
settlement in such a prohibitive location
led to its final closure in 1998.

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:57.890
Coal mining was also conducted on Hashima,
also called Gunkanjima, literally "warship

00:11:57.890 --> 00:12:02.880
island", because of the distinctive shape
given to it by the concrete and steel buildings

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:08.430
there, and located about 20 kilometers away
from the port of Nagasaki, Japan.

00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:17.370
In 1959, an area of just 6.5 hectares came
to house 5259 people, recording the highest

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:20.060
population density in history to date.

00:12:20.060 --> 00:12:25.550
Not bad for a coal mine on the water that
closed its doors forever in 1974, when Mitsubishi

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:28.490
decided to focus on oil as an energy source.

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:33.970
Another remarkable ghost village is surely
Fordlandia, lost in the Amazon rainforest.

00:12:33.970 --> 00:12:39.820
The birthplace of this town was, in 1928,
Henry Ford himself, who had decided to look

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:45.320
there for a source of cheap latex to bypass
the Sri-Lanka rubber monopoly maintained by

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:50.750
Britain, securing a direct and alternative
source of material for making tires.

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:54.529
This would contain the production costs of
the new Model A cars.

00:12:54.529 --> 00:12:59.470
The investment wouldn’t only have economic
but also social significance, because it carried

00:12:59.470 --> 00:13:05.270
with it Ford's desire to perform what was
later called "a work of civilization," aimed

00:13:05.270 --> 00:13:08.940
at "helping to develop that wonderful and
fertile land."

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:14.230
Good intentions, however, had to contend with
the difficulty of standardizing the cultivation

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:19.690
of rubber trees, because planting them too
close together made them exposed to disease

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:20.790
and pests.

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:26.120
In addition, the chosen site made it difficult
to transport raw materials and facilitated

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:30.570
water stagnation, an ideal environment for
the spread of malaria.

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:36.750
To make matters worse, despite the high salaries,
worker discontent due to the rigid work rhythms

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:42.540
that followed assembly-line philosophies resulted
in revolt in December 1930.

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:48.390
In the end Fordlandia was all talk no action,
as in 1945 Ford's grandson was forced to sell

00:13:48.390 --> 00:13:52.860
off the land to Brazil to cut down the rising
costs the company was facing.

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:55.949
At that time, World War II had come to an
end.

00:13:55.949 --> 00:13:58.000
We all know about D-Day don't we?

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:03.790
The Normandy landings, which took place on
June 6, 1944 on the French coast.

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:08.450
According to the British, Operation Overlord
wouldn’t have been possible without Tyneham,

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:12.490
a small fishing village in Dorset that "died
for England."

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:18.029
A year before the landings, in 1943, the British
government confiscated it to allow Allied

00:14:18.029 --> 00:14:22.980
forces to train on terrain considered similar
to what they would find upon arrival on the

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:23.980
continent.

00:14:23.980 --> 00:14:28.820
Even if Churchill assured residents that they
would be able to return to their homes when

00:14:28.820 --> 00:14:34.620
hostilities ceased, in 1948, with the Cold
War looming, it was decided to prioritize

00:14:34.620 --> 00:14:39.540
defensive needs and so the state took over
Tyneham once and for all.

00:14:39.540 --> 00:14:44.410
Today the village is owned by the Ministry
of Defense and is part of the Lulworth firing

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:49.430
ranges, which is why the area can only be
visited by tourists by special permit.

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:54.360
Moving to the other side of the English Channel,
four days after the Normandy landings, on

00:14:54.360 --> 00:15:01.220
June 10, 1944, a battalion of 200 Nazi soldiers
rounded up the inhabitants of the small village

00:15:01.220 --> 00:15:06.460
of Oradour-Sur-Glane under the guise of a
simple identity check and carried out a massacre,

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:13.470
burning alive 642 people including nearly
200 children and setting fire to houses, barns

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:14.470
and garages.

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:19.980
The real motivation for the massacre was the
kidnapping of an SS commander near Limoges,

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:21.810
about 20 kilometers away.

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:26.760
Of this ghostly place, today you would find
only crumbling buildings and a museum commemorating

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:28.230
the tragic event.

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:33.930
And indeed, unfortunately, war is one of the
main generators of ghost towns, either directly

00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:37.610
or indirectly, by simple cruelty or military
interests.

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:43.040
Take the case of Varosha, once a booming tourist
district of the Cypriot city of Famagusta,

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:48.800
which at its peak was home to 39,000 residents
and which, after the invasion of Cyprus by

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:55.360
the Turkish military in July 1974, became
home to decaying buildings and crumbling hotels

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:57.350
cradled by a desolate beach.

00:15:57.350 --> 00:16:02.220
In fact, in the aftermath of the invasion,
the local Greek Cypriot population fled, and

00:16:02.220 --> 00:16:07.360
since then, no one has set foot there again,
except the Turkish military of course, since

00:16:07.360 --> 00:16:10.680
today the area belongs de facto to the Republic
of Turkey.

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:16.389
In late 2020, however, the Turkish government,
which is pressing for international recognition

00:16:16.389 --> 00:16:22.319
of Northern Cyprus, announced an initiative
to revive the old tourist town, until recently

00:16:22.319 --> 00:16:25.529
unoccupied and classified as a military zone.

00:16:25.529 --> 00:16:31.779
In one year, some 400,000 civilians would
visit it, and last October Ersin Tatar, president

00:16:31.779 --> 00:16:37.240
of the self-proclaimed Turkish Republic of
Northern Cyprus, announced that Varosha would

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:39.360
also house public buildings.

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:44.750
And there you have it, depending on the interests
of the moment, beyond tourism, one can imagine

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:49.290
that a ghost town could be repopulated and
return to full operation.

00:16:49.290 --> 00:16:53.399
Then we have the phenomenon of ghost towns
in China, which is quite unique.

00:16:53.399 --> 00:16:54.399
Let me explain.

00:16:54.399 --> 00:17:00.769
Let's consider Kangbashi, in China's Inner
Mongolia Autonomous Region, about 560 kilometers

00:17:00.769 --> 00:17:02.220
west of Beijing.

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:07.250
It’s part of Ordos Prefecture, which has
a total population of 2 million, and together

00:17:07.250 --> 00:17:11.939
with the urban core of Dongsheng is one of
the two largest municipalities.

00:17:11.939 --> 00:17:17.360
The original plan was to build a boomtown
capable of housing one million people--a number

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:21.360
later scaled back to 300,000 (three hundred
thousand)--most of whom would work in the

00:17:21.360 --> 00:17:23.010
nearby coal mines.

00:17:23.010 --> 00:17:28.350
To be precise, the idea was to make Kangbashi
the new administrative center of Ordos Prefecture,

00:17:28.350 --> 00:17:34.470
and government offices, medical facilities
and schools would be relocated to nearby Dongsheng.

00:17:34.470 --> 00:17:52.770
To be precise, the idea was to make Kangbashi
the new administrative center of Ordos Prefecture,

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:59.490
and government offices, medical facilities,
and schools would be relocated to nearby Dongsheng.

00:17:59.490 --> 00:18:04.570
The reality we are witnessing today is that
the new and expanding town is not quite empty,

00:18:04.570 --> 00:18:11.650
but rather in 2016 boasted a substantial daytime
population, 100000 people of whom 80 percent

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:13.549
were full-time residents.

00:18:13.549 --> 00:18:17.230
Not a bad result when compared to Chinese
housing standards.

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:23.400
Even so, photos show us endless rows of buildings
with no apparent sign of human life.

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:28.030
This is because there is a real culture of
real estate investment in China, due to the

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:33.100
widespread belief that this is the best way
to generate and preserve wealth.

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:38.520
What on the surface might look like derelict
cities are instead simply unoccupied, then

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:43.980
filled with new housing units purchased as
investments, also made by taking advantage

00:18:43.980 --> 00:18:49.040
of government benefits, and remaining unoccupied
by owners or tenants.

00:18:49.040 --> 00:18:54.450
Think that in all of China there are about
50 municipalities that are practically unoccupied

00:18:54.450 --> 00:19:00.620
in proportion to their housing capacity, which
translates into 50 million homes without tenants,

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:03.309
according to reports by the South China Morning
Post.

00:19:03.309 --> 00:19:07.600
The problem is that the housing sector is
a pillar of China's economy, worth about a

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:10.370
quarter of all the country's economic output.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:15.270
Some believe there is a housing market bubble,
that is, a phenomenon of rising house prices,

00:19:15.270 --> 00:19:20.130
which could collapse and bring the entire
national economy into the abyss.

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:24.850
Financial uncertainty is already affecting
Evergrande, one of the real estate development

00:19:24.850 --> 00:19:32.290
giants, which has debts of $300 billion and
has about 1.6 million unsold apartments.

00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:37.120
This is the result of decades of failed urban
planning projects, the highest expression

00:19:37.120 --> 00:19:44.280
of which is the $9 billion theme park left
to rot in the city of Lu'an, located 500km

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:49.950
west of Shanghai, along with an electric car
factory that never went into operation.

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:55.710
And there you have it, the genesis of a post-apocalyptic
scenario...even before an apocalypse.

00:19:55.710 --> 00:20:01.390
Despite everything, Xi Jinping's entourage
continues to commission ambitious urban projects

00:20:01.390 --> 00:20:08.410
such as Xiong'an, a new, futuristic, hyper-technological
urban area southwest of Beijing, and all we

00:20:08.410 --> 00:20:14.549
have to do is wait to see if the Communist
Party's vision will bear fruit or prove unsuccessful.

00:20:14.549 --> 00:20:19.570
Another matter that is unclear to me is related
to Naypyidaw, the capital of Myanmar since

00:20:19.570 --> 00:20:20.669
November 6, 2005.

00:20:20.669 --> 00:20:25.670
The "king's residence"-that is the meaning
of the name-is located in the middle of the

00:20:25.670 --> 00:20:31.770
jungle, is six times the size of New York
City, cost four billion dollars, has eight-lane

00:20:31.770 --> 00:20:37.990
roads, luxury hotels, thirty government buildings
protected by a ditch, a giant golden pagoda,

00:20:37.990 --> 00:20:40.070
and four huge golf courses.

00:20:40.070 --> 00:20:41.559
Spectacular, on the surface.

00:20:41.559 --> 00:20:46.590
I wonder, however, where its lifeblood is,
since it can't get to a million inhabitants.

00:20:46.590 --> 00:20:51.150
The most certain thing at the moment is that
the former capital Yangon, which is about

00:20:51.150 --> 00:20:57.450
300km away, remains the de facto cultural
and spiritual center of the country, making

00:20:57.450 --> 00:21:00.430
the glitzy Naypyidaw a mere white elephant.

00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:06.350
Oh I forgot, at least those huge roads were
used for an episode of Top Gear, that's something.

00:21:06.350 --> 00:21:10.539
And with this last example we have come to
the end of our journey of discovery of grim

00:21:10.539 --> 00:21:11.950
and peculiar places.

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:14.260
I'm sure I've forgotten many other ghost towns.

00:21:14.260 --> 00:21:18.630
So, let me know what other places you think
are worthy of inclusion within this spooky

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:19.630
list.

00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:22.200
Thank you all for your attention and we’ll
see you in the next video.

00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:22.559
Ciao!

